  "body": "\r\nThere are image codecs that are supported in (some) browsers where those browsers (probably?) do magic sniffing to figure out the media type.\r\nThe following ones do not seem to be covered by the current mimesniff spec:\r\n\r\n- JPEG 2000, supported in all versions of Safari\r\n- JPEG XR (aka WDP, HD Photo, and Windows Media Photo), supported in Internet Explorer and in old versions of Edge\r\n- JPEG XL, supported behind a flag in Chromium and Firefox\r\n- AVIF, supported in Chromium and behind a flag in Firefox\r\n",
